lines+=section(4,'Curricular boundary','Selected skills cover SRPC movement/shift, vertical LRPC, natural-rate changes, actual/expected/unexpected inflation, adaptive updating, credibility, contract adjustment, disinflation paths, sacrifice ratios and AD-AS transfer. Rational-expectations reasoning was present through credibility/information effects but not explicitly named; a targeted existing Hard credibility question now states the available-information framework without equating it to perfect forecasting.','The live selected skills define scope. Underlying monetary tools/transmission, AD-AS/fiscal mechanisms, loanable funds, Open Economy, Micro and Managerial modules are protected. No hysteresis, new monetary machinery or advanced estimation objective was imported.')
lines+=section(5,'Prior-audit protections','All 144 nonselected concept definitions remain identical. This includes the 466 core AD-AS/fiscal records in nine modules, the 818 Money/Banking records in 13 modules and the 268 Saving/Investment records in seven modules. Each mask has zero shared authoritative IDs with these five concepts. Current modules matched the completed prior snapshots; all three prior artifact directories are hash-guarded. No cross-model exception outside Phillips scope was needed.')
lines+=section(6,'Before/after accounting','The mutually exclusive dispositions below sum to 262. A content revision may also repair an image and accessibility. A legacy reference plus evidence correction is counted as accessibility-only if the stem/key/options/feedback are unchanged; it is not also counted as path-only. `record-actions.json` dispositions every ID; `accounting.json` supplies all grouped counts.')
