lines+=section(28,'Economic/numerical defects corrected','Corrected the “ever-larger surprises” assertion, incompatible continuous-target/natural-return endpoints, expectations-only graph diagnosis without exclusions, demand-boom feedback on a supply-shock sequence, and missing initial-equilibrium/zero-offset conditions. Credible disinflation now has explicit contract-timing assumptions.','Measurement clarifications establish constant annual potential output, below-potential loss signs and cumulative rather than single-year percentages. Upper numerical replacements are original inverse/comparison tasks; they are not allegations that all prior arithmetic was wrong. Every final quantitative revision has an independent derivation.')
lines+=section(29,'Accessibility and path defects corrected','All 42 legacy references now point to registered per-concept images and receive their correct detailed evidence. Four distinct numerical-graph contracts are expanded across ten concept-level metadata entries. Fifty-six records are accessibility-only, including path repairs; ten graph records also have content revisions. Thus path-only accounting is zero even though 42 paths were corrected.','Descriptions supply axes, labels, coordinates, curve membership and guides, not the expected-inflation or policy conclusion. Existing correct detailed symbolic contracts are preserved. No source image was edited, and no accessibility was weakened to increase difficulty.')
lines+=section(30,'Final-exam calibration','The verified ECO 2251 Final Exam provides reasoning standards: no permanent tradeoff, vertical LRPC, short/long-run graph transitions, rational/adaptive expectations, structural shifts, sacrifice arithmetic and demand surprises. These already appear by Hard in the bank. Selected Hard and upper revisions improve application rather than shifting tiers.','No exam diagram, B/C/D/E/F arrangement, demographic scenario, sacrifice-ratio example, answer pattern or cosmetic rewrite was created. Existing library graphs are retained. All revised stems/options/feedback passed a new 12-word overlap screen plus human task comparison; lexical screening is not treated as proof of originality.')
lines+=section(31,'Mode readiness','All ten modes retain identical readiness for both the five-concept audit selection and the complete 14-concept parent preset. The scoped composition has no errors, 262 verified answer hashes, 24 Trial-by-Graph records, and 171 records eligible for each of Fading Fortune and Risk & Reward. The parent preset remains 728 records with unchanged counts.')
